{"id": "q012", "split": "test", "mode": "rag", "version": "7cb1b414db4c", "question": "My Pod uses two volumes and is stuck: the first volume was created somewhere without room for the second. Will the scheduler sort this out on its own?", "gold": "No, manual intervention is needed (e.g. increase capacity or delete the already-created volume)", "answerable": true, "source_file": "concepts/storage/storage-capacity.md", "retrieved": [{"chunk_id": "concepts/storage/storage-capacity.md#1", "doc_path": "concepts/storage/storage-capacity.md", "score": 0.2746818959712982, "n_tokens": 509}, {"chunk_id": "concepts/storage/storage-capacity.md#0", "doc_path": "concepts/storage/storage-capacity.md", "score": 0.24523504078388214, "n_tokens": 510}, {"chunk_id": "concepts/cluster-administration/node-shutdown.md#6", "doc_path": "concepts/cluster-administration/node-shutdown.md", "score": 0.20814357697963715, "n_tokens": 510}], "page_in_top3": true, "evidence_in_top3": true, "answer": "No – the scheduler will not resolve it automatically. The documentation says that when a Pod uses multiple volumes, one volume may be created in a topology segment that then lacks capacity for the second volume, and manual intervention (e.g., increasing capacity or deleting the first volume) is required.", "answer_usage": {"text": "No – the scheduler will not resolve it automatically. The documentation says that when a Pod uses multiple volumes, one volume may be created in a topology segment that then lacks capacity for the second volume, and manual intervention (e.g., increasing capacity or deleting the first volume) is required.", "finish_reason": "stop", "prompt_tokens": 1648, "completion_tokens": 144, "total_tokens": 1792, "calls": 1, "errors": []}, "label": "CORRECT", "judge": {"label": "CORRECT", "raw": "CORRECT", "total_tokens": 359, "calls": 1, "errors": []}}
